{"t": 1794105383.8580668, "kind": "call", "tool": "slack_post_message", "args": {"channel_id": "C07INCID003", "text": "reports-api 502s \u2014 root cause found and fixed in code.\n\nCause: upstream ledger 2026.11 now adds a `currency` field to every row. reports/export.py had a hardcoded CSV field list (`id`, `amount`), so csv.DictWriter raised `ValueError: dict contains fields not in fieldnames: 'currency'` on every export, which surfaced as 502s.\n\nFix: reports/export.py now exports `id,amount,currency` and ignores additive unknown fields so future upstream schema additions don't break the API. Reproduced the original ValueError locally and verified the fix with rows with/without currency.\n\nNext: deploy reports-api and confirm exports return 200. No data was lost; only the export endpoint was failing."}, "ok": true}
